entries[435850] = { ["name"] = "Sporefused Mycobloom", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nMycobloom is an extremely common fungus found on Khaz Algar. It can be found in practically any terrain, growing absolutely anywhere it can.\n\nThe underground of Khaz Algar is filled with a menagerie of lifeforms, large and small, each with their own unique features and behaviors.\n\nOne such lifeform is a species of magical spore, not too dissimilar from the ones found in Zaralek Cavern on the Dragon Isles. These spores, however, aren't as symbiotic.\n\nGathering an herb that hosts these spores will grant some Viridescent Spores, but have also been noted to cause strange hallucinations. Proceed with caution.\nDiscovery:\nFound somewhere on Khaz Algar" }
entries[435851] = { ["name"] = "Camouflaged Mycobloom", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nMycobloom is an extremely common fungus found on Khaz Algar. It can be found in practically any terrain, growing absolutely anywhere it can.\n\nHerbs on Khaz Algar have taken on many different variations to adapt to their environment, but one evolution stands out as particularly fascinating.\n\nThese herbs are camouflaged; completely invisible to the unassisted eye! Aspiring herbalists and alchemists have found ways to see them, but the fact that they managed to go undetected for so long is nothing short of astounding.\n\nWhile they have no extra usable materials to speak of, the herbs themselves are just as useful as their less roguish counterparts.\nDiscovery:\nFound somewhere on Khaz Algar" }
